      "biography": "Jacob E. Meusch was appointed as a temporary immigration judge to begin hearing cases in October 2026. Judge Meusch earned a Bachelor of Arts in 2007 from Creighton University, a Juris Doctor in 2010 from the University of Iowa College of Law, a Master of Laws in 2019 from the University of Virginia School of Law, and a Master of Arts in 2020 from the Naval War College. Judge Meusch has been on active duty in the U.S. Navy since 2010 and holds the rank of commander. From August 2023 to September 2026, he served as the chief and deputy chief special trial counsel at the Office of Special Trial Counsel, Detachments Bremerton and Pearl Harbor in Bremerton, Washington. From August 2022 to August 2023, he was a military prosecutor at Region Legal Service Office, Northwest in Bremerton, Washington. From June 2019 to July 2022, he served as a military defense counsel at the Military Commissions Defense Organization in Washington D.C. From 2016 to 2018, he served as an appellate defense counsel at the Navy Appellate Defense Division in Washington, D.C. From 2015 to 2016, he served as a law clerk at the Navy-Marine Corps Court of Criminal Appeals in Washington, D.C. From 2013 to 2015, he served as the staff judge advocate for Commander, Fleet Activities Sasebo in Sasebo, Japan. From 2012 to 2013, he served as a military defense counsel at Defense Service Office Southeast in Norfolk, Virginia. From 2010 to 2012, he served as a legal assistance attorney and military defense counsel at Naval Legal Service Office Mid- Atlantic in Norfolk, Virginia. Judge Meusch is a member of the Illinois State Bar and Nebraska State Bar.",
